  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Michael King made this game look small. Seven shutout innings, one hit, eight strikeouts. He took the drama out of the room before the lineup even had to show up.",
    "what_this_means": "The offense got what it needed and nothing more. Machado and Tatis each hit one, and the Padres moved to 2-0 at home by walking into two early runs and three more in the fifth. They left seven on base and struck out seven times, but they didn't have to be perfect. King's line made imperfection invisible. Matsui and Musgrove closed it out cleanly, two perfect innings between them. This is what balance looks like in the standings. Pitching locks the door so thoroughly that the offense can be human and it still doesn't matter. The bats can be sloppy because the staff isn't. That math works until someone expects the lineup to carry a tight game.",
    "what_to_watch": "Kevin Gausman takes the mound tonight with a 4.51 ERA. The kind of number that invites contact. Nick Pivetta has thrown to a 1.48 ERA over his last four starts and will be tested against a Chicago team that has nothing to lose in the final days of September.",
